%S A354935 3,6,8,11,13,16,23,26,31,36,41,43,46,51,53,56,61,71,73,81,83,86,91,96,
%T A354935 101,103,106,113,116,121,128,131,141,146,151,163,166,171,173,176,181,
%U A354935 191,193,196,206,211,223,226,233,241,243,251,256,263,271,276,281,283,293,301,311,313,321,326,331,343,346,353,356,361
%N A354935 Row 5 of A354940: Numbers k for which A345992(k) = 5, divided by 5.
%C A354935 Apparently, all terms are either of the form 5k+1 (in A016861), or of the form 5k+3 (in A016885).
%C A354935 From _Robert Israel_, Oct 16 2026: (Start)
%C A354935 This is correct.  Let m = A344005(5*k), the least m such that 5*k | m*(m+1).
%C A354935 Thus k is a term if and only if gcd(5*k,m) = 5.
%C A354935 If k is a term and 5 | k, then 25 | 5*k so 25 | m*(m+1) and therefore 25 | m or 25 | m+1.  But the first case would make 25 | gcd(5*k,m) while the second would make gcd(5*k,m) coprime to 5.  So k is not divisible by 5.
%C A354935 Suppose a term k is divisible by prime power p^j; we know p can't be 5.  If p | m then p | gcd(5*k, m), so we must have p^j | m+1. Since this is true for all prime powers dividing k, we must have k | m+1. Let m+1 = b*k. Since 5 | m, b*k == 1 (mod 5).
%C A354935 If k == 2 (mod 5), b == 3 (mod 5), and in particular m >= 3*k-1. But m' = 2*k is a smaller number such that 5*k | m'*(m'+1), as k|m' and 5|m'+1 (because m' == 2*2 = 4 (mod 5)).  So this case is impossible.
%C A354935 If k == 4 (mod 5), b == 4 (mod 5), and in particular m >= 4*k-1.  But m' = k is a smaller number such that 5*k | m'*(m'+1), as k|m' and 5|m'+1.  So this case too is impossible.  The only remaining possibilities are k == 1 or 3 (mod 5). (End)
%H A354935 Robert Israel, <a href="/A354935/b354935.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%p A354935 filter:= proc(n) local m;
%p A354935   for m from 1 do if m*(m+1) mod (5*n) = 0 then return igcd(5*n,m) = 5 fi od
%p A354935 end proc:
%p A354935 select(filter, [seq(seq(5*i+j, j=[1,3]),i=0..100)]); # _Robert Israel_, Oct 16 2026
%t A354935 q[n_] := Module[{m = 1}, While[!Divisible[m*(m + 1), 5*n], m++]; GCD[5*n, m] == 5]; Select[Range[360], q] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Jun 17 2022 *)
%o A354935 (PARI) A354935(n) = A354940sq(5,n);
%Y A354935 Row 5 of A354940.
%Y A354935 Cf. A016861, A016885, A344005, A345992.
%K A354935 nonn,changed
